    <title>
        Make authors searchable and stars visible
    </title>
    <updated>2026-10-17T13:18:39Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://2.gravatar.com/avatar/fa3ee690bbfd88026fbe7b722c11e7d8?d=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.githubassets.com%2Fimages%2Fgravatars%2Fgravatar-user-420.png&amp;r=g&amp;s=30"/>
    <author>
      <name></name>
      <email>dsh-user@users.noreply.github.com</email>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;Make authors searchable and stars visible

- resolve author from manifest, maintainers, repository owner, or npm scope:
  coverage goes from 40% to 99.9%, so author search actually works
- match stars by package basename when the catalog records a package under a
  GitHub source, which is why some packages showed no stars
- expose heat as labels (stars/downloads tiers): format 1 shows labels on the
  card but never renders sortKeys values, so a tier label is the only way to
  surface popularity in the list view&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
